SUMMARY:Switch Theatre Company Presents August Wilson's Radio Golf
DESCRIPTION:Harmond Wilks is on the verge of becoming Pittsburgh’s first Black mayor\, and his ambitious redevelopment project for the Hill District – including a new golf course – promises economic growth and a new future. But his plans may be derailed by a single rundown house owned by long time resident “Old Joe” Barlow\, who may have a deeper connection to Harmond’s past. Along with his upwardly-mobile business partner Roosevelt\, his public relations mastermind wife Mame\, and street-smart handyman Sterling\, Harmond is forced to confront the cost of progress\, the meaning of legacy\, and the value of community. The riveting final chapter of August Wilson’s 10-play American Century Cycle\, Radio Golf is a compelling and timely drama that challenges us to consider what we are willing to sacrifice for the sake of the future.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/switch-theatre-company-presents-august-wilsons-radio-golf/
LOCATION:Durham Arts Council\, 120 Morris Street\, DURHAM\, NC\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Performance,Theater
